tag-version-prefix=""
# allowScripts/denyScripts (package.json) are honored only by npm >= 11.16.0.
# We intentionally do NOT set engine-strict=true here. Doing so made `npm install`
# fail with EBADENGINE under older npm, which broke Obsidian's plugin submission
# checker: it installs with an npm older than 11.16.0, so the install aborted and
# the `obsidian` devDependency never landed — every Obsidian API then read as `any`
# and the @typescript-eslint/no-unsafe-* rules flooded with thousands of false
# positives. npm 11.16.0 is still enforced where it actually matters: via the
# `packageManager` field (corepack) and the CI pin (`npm install -g npm@11.16.0`).